{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Ms. ___ . I'm Dr. ___ , one of your hospital doctors. I see you came in with very high blood sugar and a fever yesterday. Can you tell me how you’ve been feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I felt really bad yesterday. My blood sugar was over 800 when EMS came. I didn’t take my insulin because I got confused about the time. And my foot has been hurting more."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You also had a fever and some drainage from your left heel ulcer. We’re concerned the infection might be getting into the bone. Did the doctors in the ER start any antibiotics before you left?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "They gave me something in the IV and told me to get antibiotics, but I didn’t fill the prescription. I’ve been so overwhelmed with everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:20:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s okay. We’ve started you on IV antibiotics here—Vancomycin, Cefepime, and Flagyl—to cover possible bone infection. We also gave you insulin to bring your sugar down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:21:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need surgery for my foot? I’m scared of that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:22:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The vascular surgeon and podiatry team have looked at your case. Because of poor blood flow and the exposed bone, they’re recommending a below-the-knee amputation to stop the infection from spreading."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no… that’s a lot to take in. Can’t we just keep treating it with antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:25:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can try antibiotics for now, but the infection may not heal without removing the affected area. The team wants to schedule surgery in a few weeks. You’ll go home first to think about it and follow up with them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:26:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay… I just want to go home. But I don’t want the infection to come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:27:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll make sure you’re protected. You’ll continue Vancomycin during dialysis and take Cipro and Flagyl by mouth. Blood cultures haven’t grown anything, which is a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my sugar? I usually have help with my meds, but my nurse didn’t come yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:30:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve restarted your NPH insulin—30 units in the morning—and a sliding scale for corrections. Your sugars are coming down. We’ll keep that plan unless they drop too low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. My mouth feels dry and I see white patches. Is that from the sugar?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:32:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s oral thrush, a yeast infection from high sugar and recent antibiotics. We’ll give you Nystatin swish and swallow to treat it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ve also been constipated. No bowel movement in days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2170-04-18 10:35:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see you’re on Senna and Docusate. We’ll make sure you keep taking those. Staying regular helps with overall comfort and healing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2170-04-18 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Your labs show your hemoglobin dropped a bit, but you’re not losing blood anywhere. It’s likely from your kidney disease. You’ll get your usual Aranesp during dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2170-04-18 14:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that why I feel so tired?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2170-04-18 14:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partly. Anemia can cause fatigue, but so can infection and poor sleep. As you heal, your energy should improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2170-04-18 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my heart? I know I’m not on Coumadin anymore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2170-04-18 14:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re right. You were off it due to concern for calciphylaxis, but dermatology didn’t see signs of that. Your CHADS2VASc score is high, so your outpatient team should restart anticoagulation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2170-04-18 14:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll talk to them. I don’t want a stroke."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2170-04-19 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You had dialysis yesterday and tolerated it well. Your creatinine is coming down—from 3.8 to 2.2—so your kidneys are clearing things better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2170-04-19 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. How’s my foot looking?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2170-04-19 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The ulcer is still there with exposed bone, but no new redness or swelling. The antibiotics are helping control the infection while you decide on surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2170-04-19 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been thinking… I want to go home. Can I manage the antibiotics there?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2170-04-19 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’ll get a three-week supply of Cipro and Flagyl, and Vancomycin during dialysis. A nurse will help you at home. Dr. ___’s office will contact you to plan surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2170-04-19 09:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my pain? It’s better with the Dilaudid, but I don’t want to overuse it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2170-04-19 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send home a small supply for severe pain. Continue Gabapentin and Tylenol for nerve pain. Use the Dilaudid only when needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2170-04-19 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing—we did a urine test and found yeast, but you’re not having symptoms, so we won’t treat it now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2170-04-19 13:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from the antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2170-04-19 13:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely. Antibiotics can disrupt normal balance. We’ll watch it, but no treatment is needed unless you develop symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2170-04-20 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—your blood work looks stable. White count is down, sugars are controlled, and no fever. We think you’re ready to go home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2170-04-20 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. What about my bladder? I hate straight cathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2170-04-20 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We catheterized you this morning. Because you’ve had retention before, we recommend doing it every few days. Call Dr. ___ by tomorrow to discuss how often."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2170-04-20 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll call. And I’ll weigh myself daily like last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2170-04-20 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Call if you gain more than three pounds. Keep the wound clean, take all meds, and follow up with podiatry and vascular surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2170-04-20 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’m scared about the surgery, but I know it might be necessary."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2170-04-20 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely understandable. Take your time. The team will support you every step of the way."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2170-04-20 08:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you for explaining everything. I feel more prepared now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2170-04-20 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’re here to help. A nurse will come by with your prescriptions and wound care instructions before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2170-04-20 08:11:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2170-04-20 08:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll get everything arranged. Rest, stay on top of your meds, and don’t hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2170-04-20 08:13:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2170-04-20 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Ms. ___. We’ll see you in follow-up soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2170-04-18 10:08:00",
    "admission_end": "2170-04-20 15:10:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes, end-stage renal disease on dialysis, heart failure with preserved ejection fraction, and a history of diabetic foot ulcers was admitted for hyperglycemia and fever. She had recently left the ED against medical advice but returned after her blood sugar exceeded 800 mg/dL. Evaluation revealed exposed calcaneal bone and gas on imaging, concerning for osteomyelitis. She was started on IV Vancomycin, Cefepime, and Flagyl. Vascular surgery recommended a below-the-knee amputation due to poor perfusion, but the patient opted to return home to consider the decision. She was discharged on oral Ciprofloxacin and Metronidazole, with continued Vancomycin during dialysis. Her blood glucose was stabilized on her home insulin regimen, and she received Nystatin for oral thrush. She was instructed to perform intermittent straight catheterization and to follow up with podiatry and vascular surgery for surgical planning.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with peripheral circulatory disorders, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Ulcer of heel and midfoot",
      "Unspecified osteomyelitis, ankle and foot",
      "Candidiasis of mouth",
      "Congestive heart failure, unspecified",
      "Atrial fibrillation",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Anemia in chronic kidney disease"
    ]
  }
}
